# Backup Recovery Runbook
<!-- {{ ansible_managed }} -->

## Overview
This runbook documents the backup recovery procedures for {{ ansible_hostname | default('this system') }}.

## Backup Location
- **Primary**: {{ backup_source_dir | default('/var/backup') }}
- **Test Directory**: /var/backup/test

## Recovery Procedures

### 1. Locate Latest Backup
```bash
ls -la {{ backup_source_dir | default('/var/backup') }}/*.tar.gz | head -5
```

### 2. Verify Backup Integrity
```bash
tar -tzf /path/to/backup.tar.gz > /dev/null && echo "OK" || echo "CORRUPTED"
```

### 3. Extract Backup
```bash
# Extract to temporary location first
mkdir -p /tmp/restore-test
tar -xzf /path/to/backup.tar.gz -C /tmp/restore-test

# Verify contents
ls -la /tmp/restore-test/
```

### 4. Restore Data
```bash
# Stop relevant services first
systemctl stop <service-name>

# Restore files
cp -a /tmp/restore-test/* /target/location/

# Fix permissions if needed
chown -R <user>:<group> /target/location/

# Restart services
systemctl start <service-name>
```

## Automated Testing
- **Schedule**: Weekly (Sunday 2:00 AM)
- **Script**: /usr/local/bin/backup-verify.sh
- **Logs**: /var/log/backup-test.log

